-- Half Dome day 1 (Happy Isles -> Little Yosemite Valley) was still a
-- 5-point hand-researched approximation -- OSM tags this corridor across
-- many short 'Mist Trail' and 'John Muir Trail' way fragments that don't
-- connect at either the Happy Isles or LYV end when chain-matched from the
-- Happy Isles side (the greedy walk picks a dead-end JMT branch among the
-- many fragments there); seeding the identical search from the LYV side
-- instead finds the one connected route through both trails' fragments,
-- confirmed by a smooth, monotonically-ascending elevation profile.
-- Caveat: it falls ~900m short of the exact Happy Isles trailhead pin (a
-- real gap in OSM's way network there, not a matching error), and it is
-- the same underlying trail data as day 2's return leg (0009), reversed --
-- not a distinct pure-Mist-Trail variant, since Mist-Trail-tagged fragments
-- alone don't reach either endpoint. Still a large accuracy improvement
-- over the prior 5-point approximation, which is why this is applied.
-- Day 2's return leg (0009) is also re-applied here from a more targeted
-- named-way query than the original pipeline's generic bbox pull, though
-- its geometry is very close to what was already there.
